    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "correctAnswerText": "Ketamine",
    "explanation": "A perfect agent should decrease cerebral blood flow and cerebral metabolic rate of oxygen. With the use of inhaled agents, this association gets uncoupled. IV sedatives, narcotics, and hypnotics tend to decrease cerebral blood flow and metabolic rate of oxygen except for ketamine, which increases both.",
    "source": "Advanced Knowledge Assessment in Pediatric Critical Care 2024",
